In 2008, Fyffe was nominated for best newcomer at the [[MOBO Awards]], winning two awards: Best UK Newcomer and Best Hip-Hop act.<ref name="MOBO08">{{cite web|url=http://www.zimbio.com/pictures/zNP7l5ZDR_w/MOBO+Awards+2008+Winners+Boards/AlD_JumlbYF/Chipmunk|title=MOBO Awards 2008–Winners Boards (Chipmunk)|publisher=Zimbio|access-date=16 June 2009}}</ref> He also won Best Hip-Hop Act at the MOBO Awards 2009.<ref name="MoveOver">{{cite news|url=http://entertainment.timesonline.co.uk/tol/arts_and_entertainment/music/article6856049.ece|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110617002317/http://entertainment.timesonline.co.uk/tol/arts_and_entertainment/music/article6856049.ece|url-status=dead|archive-date=17 June 2011|title=Move over Kanye, as Chipmunk from Tottenham crowned king of Mobo awards|newspaper=[[Times Online]]|date=1 October 2009|access-date=13 November 2010|location=London|first=Patrick|last=Foster}}</ref> He also won an award with [[Emeli Sandé]] for Best British Single for their song "[[Diamond Rings (song)|Diamond Rings]]".<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bet.com/tag/ho898f/chipmunk |title=Chipmunk |publisher=BET |access-date=21 December 2011}}</ref> The same year, Fyffe won an MP3 Award at the MP3 Music Awards 2009 for "Diamond Rings",<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.mtv.co.uk/news/kings-of-leon/164814-mp3-music-award-winners-announced |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110807151535/http://www.mtv.co.uk/news/kings-of-leon/164814-mp3-music-award-winners-announced |url-status=dead |archive-date=7 August 2011 |title=MP3 Music Award Winners Announced &#124; Kings Of Leon &#124; News |publisher=Mtv.co.uk |date=13 November 2009 |access-date=21 December 2011}}</ref> which was published and promoted by [[MTV Network]]. 

